Scope, and whose work is whose
==============================

This repository distributes BUILDS, not tools. The CIAs attached to its releases
are installable patches for games you must already own.

Nothing here grants any rights to:

  * Dai Gyakuten Saiban: Naruhodou Ryuunosuke no Bouken (3DS, 2015)
  * Dai Gyakuten Saiban 2: Naruhodou Ryuunosuke no Kakugo (3DS, 2017)
  * The Great Ace Attorney Chronicles (2021)
  * any text, graphics, audio or data from any of them

All of which remain (c) Capcom.

Nor does it cover the upstream patch this is built on, which is the work of its
own author:

    https://github.com/senyarom/tgaa2-en-patch

That project ports Capcom's official English text onto the Japanese 3DS builds,
with the layout pipeline and font handling that make it possible. Everything
here sits on top of it. Where Capcom localised the DLC, the text in these
builds IS senyarom's carry of Capcom's English, word for word -- verified by
comparing against the Chronicles release directly.

Scarlet Study's earlier fan translation made the first playable English 3DS
build and was used as a reference point throughout:

    https://www.romhacking.net/translations/6510/

THE JAPANESE BASE GAMES ARE NOT DISTRIBUTED HERE, and will not be. That is the
same line the upstream project draws. You supply your own.

The update and DLC packages that ARE distributed contain Capcom's content with
English assets substituted -- the same class of artifact upstream releases:

    https://github.com/senyarom/tgaa2-en-patch/releases

If you want Capcom's translation properly, buy The Great Ace Attorney
Chronicles. It is very good, it is on every current platform, and it is the
reason any of this can exist.
